  "_straight_doc": "Ledger 0054 P3 (2026-10-18): each stub on the chord of its OSM branch over its 16 m (tools/stub_roads.py straighten): the corner returns fit one straight edge line to the stub, and side streets curving 0.3-1.2 m within their first 16 m put the stub's own road under the return's curb top (audit K / I on P3's second build)."
 },
 "_doc_p3": "Ledger 0054 P3 step 4 (2026-10-18): declared on the four north pieces as route_connectors writes them (tools/stub_roads.py declare --host north_J1_waring,north_princess_view,north_mission_gorge,north_J5_jackson_north --mouths source/expansion/routes__mouths.json --legs ...=W,P,M,J --osm data/osm.expansion.json); the J1 / J5 legs (the loop) and J3's quarry drive (the pad's own stub arm) set to skip by hand. Public side roads: a 15 m stub to Kevin's K-rail; service ways: a curb cut.",
 "_doc_repair_1": "Ledger 0054 P3 repair round 1 (2026-10-19, the view lens: 'Glenroy St's mouths are not declared'): re-declared with --merge after tools/stub_roads.py stopped taking a short side-street way whose last nodes lie inside the host's width for a host carriageway (it must also run ALONG the host). Two public mouths that had no entry at all now have a stub: Glenroy St's south-west leg off Princess View (way 663868618) and Doreen Rd off Jackson (way 5955946); two service ways get a curb cut. Set to skip by hand: navajo_road_436270254_L (J5: the loop itself, as its two neighbours) and service_577444270_R (a 12 deg parallel lane; its 87 deg turn-in, service_577444270_R_722, keeps its curb cut). Birchwood St's second OSM way (5958459) is the 10 m crossover between Waring's two carriageways through its median, not a side street: Birchwood leaves Waring only to the north-east (stubbed).",
